; `calc on` computed `3 ∉ S` for every set `S`: only the element was a number, the set wasn't one
; of the calculator's (`Nat`, `Int`, ...) -- `3 ∈ {3}`, `3 ∉ {3}`, `false` was accepted, also with
; --strict (found by the soundness hunt, 2026-10-14; `numeric_comparison_holds`)
load natural
calc on
3 ∈ {3}
expect "ProofError"
    3 ∉ {3}
const A
expect "ProofError"
    3 ∉ A
-3 ∉ Nat                      ; a set of the calculator: computed, as before
